t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Pre-release</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Date Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">?</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t</section>\n\n\n\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<p><b>Steel Axe</b> (<i>Usually called Short Steel Axe</i>) was once an axe sold at <a href=\"/wiki/The_Oak_Depot\" title=\"The Oak Depot\">The Oak Depot</a>. It's a weaker and smaller version of the <a href=\"/wiki/Tall_Steel_Axe\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tall Steel Axe\">Tall Steel Axe</a>, and was sold next to it. The reason why it was removed, is probably due to the fact that there was too small of a difference between the two.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appearance\">Appearance</span></h2>\n<p><b>Steel Axe</b> is a small hatchet made out of wood and steel. It's headpiece is dark gray in color and uses the default legacy metal texture. Handle, like any other axe, is made out of dark brown wood with default legacy wood material applied to it. At the bottom of it there is a small hole.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trivia\">Trivia</span></h2>\n<ul><li>Originally it was named <b>Steel Axe</b>, but after v1.52.0 <b>Tall Steel Axe</b> was renamed to \"Steel Axe\"</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260903163440\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 93/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 643/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 151/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.006/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1019509/104857600 by